x86_64-windows  the case prints what name() answers, and that is the object's own string - `i`, `1D`, `PKc` from the Itanium type_info, `int`, `struct D`, `char const *` undecorated by the vcruntime from the Microsoft descriptor - so one .expected cannot serve both ABIs. `typeid` itself compiles for this target since 2026-09-26: typeid-ms.cpp is the same shapes printed as comparisons, and it runs on the box. The case also declares its own std::type_info in the Itanium layout, which is not this ABI's.
